    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Malay Muslim sultanate on the northwest coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a> whose rulers trace a line back to the fourteenth century.</li><li>Around 1500 its fleets and allies made it the leading power of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a>'s coasts and the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>.</li><li>It lost most of its lands to Sarawak and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> but survived as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> and, from 1984, an independent state.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>A king of Po-ni, early Brunei, died during a visit to the Ming court in 1408, and his tomb can still be visited in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

